#sol-item(1, "A")[
  $dif y / dif x = 3x^2 + 12x + 9 = 3(x + 1)(x + 3)$, so the stationary points are at $x = -1$ and $x = -3$. *Chapter 3.*
]

#sol-item(2, "C")[
  $dif y / dif x = 3x^2 - 16 = 3(x + 4)(x - 4)$, which is positive outside the roots $x = +-4$. *Chapter 3.*
]

#sol-item(3, "D")[
  $y'' = 6x + 0$, which at $x = 3$ equals $18 > 0$. A positive second derivative means a minimum. *Chapter 3.*
]

